I am standing in my kitchen when the doorbell rings.
I walk out into the hallway and open the door.
It is Nina, and she has a big smile on her face.
"Hello Maya, thank you so much for the invitation," she says.
She steps inside and laughs while she takes off her shoes.
I give her a warm hug.
Nina is holding a beautiful, green houseplant in her hands.
"This is for you," she says and hands me the plant.
"It fits perfectly in your living room."
"Thank you, it is really pretty," I answer happily.
I place the green plant on a small table next to the door.
Suddenly, Nina takes a deep breath.
"Wow, it smells absolutely wonderful in here," she says.
"Are those the Mexican spices?" she asks curiously.
I nod and explain that I have made a traditional stew.
"The spicy smell makes me absolutely starving," Nina laughs.
"Fortunately, the food is completely ready," I say with a smile.
We sit down at the table together to eat.
